          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.015399249183234907,
          "sentence": "The scalability claims are particularly unclear.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9846007508167651,
            "ai": 0.0008419643657069359,
            "paraphrased": 0.01455728481752797
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.01647099533553008,
          "sentence": "The paper repeatedly mentions lack of scalability as a drawback for convnets, but it appears the proposed CKM is less scalable than a standard SVM, yet SVMs often handle much fewer training instances than deep neural networks.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9835290046644699,
            "ai": 0.0008547455487279922,
            "paraphrased": 0.015616249786802091
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.016825095571209293,
          "sentence": "It appears the scalability advantages are mostly for training sets with roughly fewer than 10,000 instances -- and even if the method could scale to >> 10,000 training instances, it's unclear whether the predictive accuracy would be competitive with convnets in that domain.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9831749044287907,
            "ai": 0.0008946936977517767,
            "paraphrased": 0.015930401873457515
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.01782329853722524,
          "sentence": "Moreover, the idea of doing 10^6 operations simply for creating virtual instances on 10^4 training points and 100 test points is still somewhat daunting.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9821767014627748,
            "ai": 0.0006730599018709603,
            "paraphrased": 0.01715023863535428
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.018462476215671573,
          "sentence": "What if we had 10^6 training instances and 10^5 testing instances?",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9815375237843285,
            "ai": 0.000564321562261774,
            "paraphrased": 0.017898154653409798
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.017016967966427224,
          "sentence": "with Gaussian kernels) on modern datasets, the scalability claims in this paper need to be significantly expanded and clarified.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9829830320335727,
            "ai": 0.0005270387254647407,
            "paraphrased": 0.016489929240962483
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.016609689321475177,
          "sentence": "On a related note, the suggestion that convnets grow quadratically in computation with additional training instances in the introduction needs to be augmented with more detail, and is potentially misleading.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9833903106785248,
            "ai": 0.0005804556530656776,
            "paraphrased": 0.016029233668409498
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.016197177446299588,
          "sentence": "Convnets typically scale linearly with additional training data.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9838028225537004,
            "ai": 0.0008952463059887959,
            "paraphrased": 0.015301931140310792
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.01545597790836633,
          "sentence": "In general, the paper suffers greatly from a lack of clarity and issues of presentation.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9845440220916337,
            "ai": 0.0006236817843244444,
            "paraphrased": 0.014832296124041884
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.018203093986670343,
          "sentence": "As above, the full story is not presented, with critical details often missing.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9817969060133297,
            "ai": 0.0006761108255104561,
            "paraphrased": 0.017526983161159887
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.0186529090999596,
          "sentence": "Moreover, it would strengthen the paper to remove broad claims such as \"Just as support vector machines (SVMs) eclipsed multilayer perceptrons in the 1990s, CKMs could become a compelling alternative to convnets with reduced training time and sample complexity\", suggesting that CKMs could eclipse convolutional neural networks, and instead provide more helpful and precise information.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9813470909000404,
            "ai": 0.0022327494963497122,
            "paraphrased": 0.016420159603609888
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.004445879823589936,
          "sentence": "Convnets are multilayer perceptrons used in the 1990s (as well as now) and they are not eclipsed by SVMs -- they have different relative advantages.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9955541201764101,
            "ai": 0.004327218853658448,
            "paraphrased": 0.00011866096993148763
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.0003821302261848716,
          "sentence": "And based on the information presented, broadly advertising scalability over convnets is misleading.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9996178697738152,
            "ai": 0.000327768578918809,
            "paraphrased": 0.00005436164726606266
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.0003383519129980099,
          "sentence": "Can CKMs scale to datasets with millions of training and test instances?",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.999661648087002,
            "ai": 0.00028444674240106526,
            "paraphrased": 0.000053905170596944625
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.0002739325073913866,
          "sentence": "It seems as if the scalability advantages are limited to smaller datasets, and asymptotic scalability could be much worse in general.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9997260674926086,
            "ai": 0.00022209035624560117,
            "paraphrased": 0.000051842151145785425
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00022993782222354673,
          "sentence": "And even if CKMs could scale to such datasets would they have as good predictive accuracy as convnets on those applications?",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9997700621777764,
            "ai": 0.00017795684802124267,
            "paraphrased": 0.000051980974202304066
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00011751462382168379,
          "sentence": "Being specific and with full disclosure about the precise strengths and limitations of the work would greatly improve this paper.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9998824853761783,
            "ai": 0.00007336717142269749,
            "paraphrased": 0.0000441474523989863
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00019402530360826945,
          "sentence": "CKMs may be more robust to adversarial examples than standard convnets, due to the virtual instances.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9998059746963918,
            "ai": 0.00014682199801662612,
            "paraphrased": 0.000047203305591643314
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00015560337339279453,
          "sentence": "But there are many approaches to make deep nets more robust to adversarial examples.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9998443966266072,
            "ai": 0.00011739995792532074,
            "paraphrased": 0.000038203415467473806
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.0001372700034343352,
          "sentence": "It would be useful to consider and compare to these.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9998627299965657,
            "ai": 0.00009867842746908868,
            "paraphrased": 0.0000385915759652465
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00011493736521651105,
          "sentence": "The ideas behind CKMs also are not inherently specific to kernel methods.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9998850626347835,
            "ai": 0.00007198412499541003,
            "paraphrased": 0.000042953240221101014
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00013373838930665053,
          "sentence": "Have you considered looking at using virtual instances in a similar way with deep networks?",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9998662616106934,
            "ai": 0.00009372659541225268,
            "paraphrased": 0.00004001179389439785
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.0001281593528619475,
          "sentence": "A full exploration might be its own paper, but the idea is worth at least brief discussion in the text.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9998718406471381,
            "ai": 0.00007977079729094911,
            "paraphrased": 0.0000483885555709984
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00009595117198697267,
          "sentence": "A big advantage of SVMs (with Gaussian kernels) over deep neural nets is that one can achieve quite good performance with very little human intervention (design choices).",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.999904048828013,
            "ai": 0.00005066145666710402,
            "paraphrased": 0.00004528971531986865
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00009375959597638323,
          "sentence": "However, CKMs seem to require extensive intervention, in terms of architecture (as with a neural network), and in insuring that the virtual instances are created in a plausible manner for the particular application at hand.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
